@title Lantern Notes 3.8.0 release notes
@subtitle Released 2026-10-14

Thanks for using Lantern Notes. Here is what changed in 3.8.0.

## New

- **Shared folders.** Invite up to 25 collaborators to a folder, and choose view or edit access for each.
- **Scheduled dark mode.** Dark mode follows sunset, or a time range you set.
- **Evernote import.** Import Evernote ENEX files, including attachments up to 50 MB each.

## Improved

- Search is about twice as fast. The median query drops from 410 ms to 190 ms on a library of 10,000 notes.
- Background sync on Android uses about 18 percent less battery.

## Fixed

- Tables no longer lose column widths when exported to PDF.
- The app no longer freezes when opening a note with more than 200 images.
- Reminders fire at the right time after a daylight saving change.
- Pasted web links keep their titles.
- Dragging a note onto a folder in the sidebar works with a trackpad on Windows.
- The word count includes text inside tables.

## Known issues

- Shared folders cannot yet be used with end-to-end encrypted notebooks. This is planned for 3.9.
- ENEX import drops nested tags beyond three levels.

## Deprecations

- Windows 8.1 support ends on 2027-01-31.
- From version 3.9, the minimum Android version will be Android 10.
